                                "sense_id": "37d54ee4-53ba-37fa-8239-807dd4f45083",
                                "text": "Droitwich was then clearly more important than any of the Cheshire wiches; indeed the two most northerly of them were reported in 1086 to be \"utterly waste\", while Nantwich farm was worth only £10 a year."
